I don't like the Orb of Detection. It doesn't fit the 'scientist'
aspect of Archeologists. People confuse it with the Orb of Fate. Its
invocation power (Invisibility) can be obtained intrinsically. It isn't
even related to the Archeologist's pantheon.

In this patch the Archeologist's quest artifact, the Orb of Detection,
is replaced with an artifact more befitting the Archeologist's
Mesoamerican pantheon: the Mirror of Tezcatlipoca, a shield of
reflection.

Tezcatlipoca was the Nahuatl twin god, and rival, of Quetzalcoatl. He
possessed a mirror after which he is named.

* His mirror was used as a shield. Hence, this artifact is a shield of
reflection.
* His mirror displayed all of mankind's actions and deeds in it. Hence,
it confers ESP.
* His mirror was surrounded by flame. Hence, it also confers fire
resistance.
* His mirror, being on fire, released smoke that killed his enemies.
Hence, invoking the Mirror of Tezcatlipoca creates a stinking cloud. If
it is cursed or the player is not an Archeologist, it centers the cloud
at the player (i.e it sees you as an enemy). Otherwise, the player can
choose a location as per the stinking cloud scroll effect.
* It also halves spell damage.
* As it already confers reflection by wearing it, it does NOT confer
magic resistance.

Also, this patch allows quest nemeses to equip non-weapon quest
artifacts if they can.

Note 1: This patch overrides the object invocation property TAMING,
used by the defunct Palantir of Westernesse. Why? 'cause.

